  "title": "Why GitHub Copilot misses context (and how to fix it)",
  "description": "Out of the box, GitHub Copilot doesn't know your conventions, architecture opinions, or how you ship. But you can teach it. Set up shared rules and reusable prompts so Copilot follows your standards. Build custom agents and skills for workflows your team actually runs. Dial in settings that scale from five engineers to five hundred. Rules, skills, prompt files, custom agents — see how they fit and when to reach for each.\n\nSeating for this session is first-come, first-served. Add it to your schedule to plan your day and arrive early to secure a spot.",
